QuadriFlow, vendored for Sculpt Kit's native engine

Copied from Blender's repository, extern/quadriflow, main branch at commit
ac44e43ae514c07f153b9694e25268a34ba10727 (23 October 2026), which is upstream QuadriFlow
(https://github.com/hjwdzh/QuadriFlow, Huang, Zhou, Niessner, Shewchuk and Guibas 2018) with Blender's
patches/blender.patch applied: Boost replaced by its own patches/boykov_kolmogorov_max_flow.hpp, and
ComputeIndexMap reporting failure instead of asserting. See README.blender.

Left out: src/main.cpp (the command line), src/Optimizer.cu (CUDA), src/post-solver.cpp (unused, needs
Boost), and everything of LEMON's but its licence, its config template and the lemon/ sources this build
includes (the min-cost flow, preflow and graph headers; trimmed from the build's own dependency list).

Licences: QuadriFlow is BSD-3 (LICENSE.txt); LEMON 1.3.1 is under the Boost Software License
(3rd/lemon-1.3.1/LICENSE); pcg32 is Apache-2.0 and pss is BSD-style (headers in 3rd/). Blender's changes
are GPL-2.0-or-later. All are compatible with Sculpt Kit's GPL-3.0-or-later.

Sculpt Kit's own code that drives it is in ../../src/qflow_bridge.cpp. Changes made here, each marked
"Sculpt Kit" in the source:

- src/parametrizer-flip.cpp, Parametrizer::FixHoles(): the walk along an open edge loop turns around each
  vertex until it meets the next open edge; around a non-manifold fan it never does and looped forever (seen
  on an open vest with a frozen field). The turn is capped and that loop is skipped (left unfilled).
- src/parametrizer-mesh.cpp, Parametrizer::FixValence(): every walk around a vertex is capped at 256 turns
  and both of its repeat-until-unchanged loops at 64 rounds. Around a non-manifold fan a walk never returns
  to where it started; on a closed cast frozen to our field with sharp edges kept it ran for half an hour.
- src/parametrizer.hpp, src/parametrizer-flip.cpp: a flag_fill_holes switch (on by default, as before) around
  the two calls to FixHoles(), which fills every hole of under 25 vertices. On an open sculpt that also
  closed small real openings; the kit turns it off there and fills only the holes that do not lie on the
  sculpt's own open edges.
